spec: S02-16, S02-14, S02-07

pull never clobbers: a `.md` bound to another Document, or one without a Sidecar that differs
from what would be written, is refused (exit 5) unless `--force`; identical content is fine.
(The "edited since pull" branch is covered by `crates/annotary/tests/cli_docs.rs`, which can
edit files between steps.)

```console
$ annotary -p rowan push pg.md
pg	[..]	v1

$ annotary -p rowan push other/pg.md
pg	[..]	v1

$ annotary -p rowan pull pg.md --out other
? 5
error: pg.md here is bound to [..] — not [..] — `pull --force` overwrites it, or use --out DIR

$ annotary -p rowan pull pg.md --out other --force
pull: 0 threads, 0 assets
pg.md	pg.annotary	v1

$ annotary -p rowan pull pg.md --out loose
? 5
error: pg.md exists here without a Sidecar and differs from v1 — `pull --force` overwrites it, or use --out DIR

$ annotary -p rowan pull pg.md --out same
pull: 0 threads, 0 assets
pg.md	pg.annotary	v1

$ annotary -p rowan status same/pg.md
pg	[..]	v1	action:-	open:0	mentions-me:0	seq:[..]

```
